We will start with **direct substitution** (step A):

$\begin{align}
g(\blueD{-8})&=\dfrac{3(\blueD{-8})^2+24(\blueD{-8})}{(\blueD{-8})^2+16(\blueD{-8})+64}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{192-192}{64-128+64}
\\\\
&=\dfrac00
\end{align}$

We got the **indeterminate form** $\dfrac00$ (step D).

Now we need to determine which analytical method is applicable.

Since we have a quotient with polynomial expressions, we will use the method of **factoring** (step E):

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{3x^2+24x}{x^2+16x+64}&=\dfrac{3x\cancel{(x+8)}}{\cancel{(x+8)}(x+8)}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{3x}{x+8}
\end{align}$

Now we can try **direct substitution** (step A) once again!

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{3(\blueD{-8})}{(\blueD{-8})+8}&=\dfrac{-24}{0}
\end{align}$

We got $\dfrac{b}{0}$ where $b\neq0$.

This means that $\displaystyle\lim_{x\to -8}g(x)$ doesn't exist because there is a vertical **asymptote** at that $x$-value (step B).
